Here are two ways to do this. The first is a **simple version**, and the second is a **modern, polished version** with hover effects to make it feel like a real professional button.

### Option 1: Simple & Clean
Use this if you just want the basic colors without any fancy effects.

**HTML:**
```html
<button class="btn-simple">Click Me</button>
```

**CSS:**
```css
.btn-simple {
  background-color: #00FF00; /* Bright Green */
  color: white;              /* White Text */
  padding: 10px 20px;        /* Space around text */
  border: none;              /* Removes default border */
  cursor: pointer;           /* Changes mouse to hand icon */
  font-size: 16px;
}
```

---

### Option 2: Modern & Polished (Recommended)
This version adds rounded corners, a subtle shadow, and a "hover" effect so the user knows the button is clickable.

**HTML:**
```html
<button class="btn-modern">Get Started</button>
```

**CSS:**
```css
.btn-modern {
  /* Colors */
  background-color: #2ecc71; /* A vibrant, professional emerald green */
  color: #ffffff;            /* Pure white */

  /* Sizing and Spacing */
  padding: 12px 24px;
  font-size: 18px;
  font-weight: 600;

  /* Styling */
  border: none;
  border-radius: 8px;        /* Rounded corners */
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: all 0.3s ease; /* Smooth transition for hover effect */
